sentences.t:
nec sat rationis in armis,
sed glomerare manum bello et concurrere in arcem
cum sociis ardent animi;

sentences.l:
nor is there enough of reason in arms,
but to gather a band for battle and to run together to the citadel
with comrades burn my spirits;

sentences.t:
Arduus armatos mediis in moenibus adstans
fundit equus, victorque Sinon incendia miscet
insultans;

sentences.l:
Tall, armed men in the midst of the walls standing
the horse pours out, and victorious Sinon the fires stirs together,
exulting;

sentences.t:
per tela, per hostis
vadimus haud dubiam in mortem, mediaeque tenemus
urbis iter;

sentences.l:
through weapons, through enemies
we go to no doubtful death, and hold of the middle
city the way;

sentences.t:
inprovisum aspris veluti qui sentibus anguem
pressit humi nitens, trepidusque repente refugit
attollentem iras et caerula colla tumentem;

sentences.l:
unforeseen, in rough brambles as a snake
he who has trodden on the ground, pressing, and trembling suddenly flees from it
rearing its rage and the blue-dark neck swelling;
